| 4i | RIGHT AFTER (ruled 2026-11-18) | the words (#/rulings, 2026-11-18, the flow unblurred): `vessel seed` becomes `vessel lay` across CLI and canon, and carry's names become the keep's restore and the census drill (Lares-Alpha, backlog-alpha #/now, the lay rename landing first in `command-help.ts`); `lares wear N` and every route prompt naming whose route it asks (Lares-Awakens, Wave 4, `wear` rebasing on `lay`); oracle to floor and the founding record (Lares-Awakens, Wave 3f); pin for the floor alone, holds, the seed witness, revert, keep for the backup alone, and the 2 a.m. test on every operator-facing string (both sessions, in each lane's review); the mount-versus-worn sweep the open ledger names. BUILT: `vessel lay`, the keep's restore and the census drill (PR #232, `f694aedf4`); unnumbered schema tags (PR #232, #245); `lares wear N` with every route prompt naming whose route it asks (PR #235). Owed: oracle to floor and the founding record (Wave 3f, on the next labelled re-bake); the mount-versus-worn sweep's rest after Word-Wright's first pass (`0474ad790`, backlog-awakens #/waves) | A tired operator reads one word for one act during a rite; seed, pin, keep, carry and oracle each named two things. |

